  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> be a solution curve of the differential equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math> is:",
